        "id": "ch14_4_4-3",
        "text": "# update_port_desc.py (part 2)\npayload2 = json.dumps({\n\"fullClassName\": \"equipment.PhysicalPort\",\n\"properties\": {\n\"description\": \"description added by a Python\nprogram\"\n}\n})\nurl2 = \"https:// NFMP_URL :8443/nfm-p/rest/api/v1/\nmanagedobjects/\"+port_ofn\nresponse = requests.request(\"PUT\", url2, headers=headers,\ndata=payload2, verify=False)\nprint(response.text)\n490     Using Python for Network Automation\nNetwork automation is the process of creating and updating many network objects in\na specific order. For example, we can update a port before creating an IP connectivity\nservice to connect two or more local area networks. This type of use case requires that\nwe perform a series of tasks to update all the ports involved, as well as many other objects.\nWith the NMS API, we can orchestrate all these tasks in a program to implement an\nautomated process.\nIn the next section, we will explore how to integrate with Nokia NSP or similar systems\nfor event-driven communication.",
